From openbsd-alpha  Wed Sep 25 14:43:41 2002
From: janjaap () stack ! nl (Janjaap van Velthooven)
Date: Wed, 25 Sep 2002 14:43:41 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: more observations on Matrox Millenium II on alpha.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=103296510122540

	Hi,

I've been playing some more with a Matrox millenium 2 card on my alpha.
(curent kernel and X)

Yes it still panics the kernel but I convinced the kernel to ignore that
for now. (I wont post how to the list as I think bad practice should not
be encouraged)

It apears there are two moments during startup where the panic conditions
are triggered.

It now works mostly. but there are still some issues I would like to
mention. 

1) on exit the videomode is very garbled. 
2) changing vt's is not possible (I guess it also would be useless due
   to not being capable of setting the card do a normal (text) video mode)
3) unlike my i386 systems the backspace key actually produces a backspace...
   other than that keybord support seems improved.

	Janjaap van Velthooven

PS. thanks for the good work already done.
