From openbsd-alpha  Thu Sep 26 23:15:13 2002
From: Dries Schellekens <gwyllion () ace ! ulyssis ! org>
Date: Thu, 26 Sep 2002 23:15:13 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: GLINT/Permedia video driver works in 3.2-beta
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=103308218612494

Hey,

I just want to report that the glint driver works on my alpha with OpenBSD
3.2-beta.

Some changes I had to make to the default installation.
* Add "machdep.allowaperture=1" to /etc/sysctl.conf
* I ran X -configure. This generated /root/XF86Config.new and reported
that my mouse was not detected.
* I manually changed mouse entry to
Section "InputDevice"
        Identifier  "Mouse0"
        Driver      "mouse"
        Option      "Protocol" "wsmouse"
        Option      "Device" "/dev/wsmouse0"
EndSection
(it would be nice if X -configure was able to detect the mouse correctly)

Quite easy ;-) Thanks Matthieu.

